{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim","id":1408363,"title":"Ghosts as duguthim","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-15T09:05:52-07:00","id":1408363,"title":"Ghosts as duguthim","content":"I was planning on using an idigam out of Night Horrors Wolfsbane that basically creates duguthim using ghosts instead of spirits, however I'm not certain how to stat that. I've tried to consolidate duguthim creation with some ideas of using things out of Geist, as that's the closest I've found to ghost creation, but it's just not working in my head. And ideas? Or is there another book I should be looking at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T09:11:13-07:00","id":1408364,"title":"","content":"Spirit-Claimed and Ghost-Claimed are mechanically identical (with the exception of Ghost-Claimed not being able to cross the Gauntlet at Loci) so I don't know what you need help with. Just remember that ghosts generally have different motivations than spirits and wouldn't act quite the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T11:09:28-07:00","id":1408385,"title":"","content":"Ya, the only real difference between a ghost that claimed someone and a spirit is how you can interact with them and what realms they are tied to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T17:07:22-07:00","id":1408421,"title":"","content":"Mostly I can't seem to find how to stat a ghost itself, so I don't know how to stat it the way I would a duguthim. Can I just use spirit creation for ghosts or something? Geist basically has you create a human and then the geist itself is this ethereal concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T18:12:58-07:00","id":1408434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CritCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408421#post1408421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I can't seem to find how to stat a ghost itself, so I don't know how to stat it the way I would a duguthim. Can I just use spirit creation for ghosts or something? Geist basically has you create a human and then the geist itself is this ethereal concept.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Check the base CofD book, or look in the Ephemeral Rules section of Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:44:12-07:00","id":1408451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408434#post1408434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Check the base CofD book, or look in the Ephemeral Rules section of Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a Geist 2e that I don't know about? I'd heard one was coming out, but I didn't know it was out yet. I don't know which version is on Drive Thru RPG, either.<br /> I'll check CoD, though, and see if I just missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:51:22-07:00","id":1408453,"title":"","content":"I think I've found it in CofD? Looks very similar to stuff in Predators, so doesn't seem too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:51:39-07:00","id":1408454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CritCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408451#post1408451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Geist 2e that I don't know about? I'd heard one was coming out, but I didn't know it was out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/272090/Geist-The-SinEaters-Second-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Been out since earlier this year</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T03:02:53-07:00","id":1408468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CritCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408421#post1408421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I can't seem to find how to stat a ghost itself, so I don't know how to stat it the way I would a duguthim. Can I just use spirit creation for ghosts or something? Geist basically has you create a human and then the geist itself is this ethereal concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't bother with either version of Geist: The Sin-Eaters. The character creation process is not about regular ghosts. It's about a specific subset of ghosts that have used a very different type of Manifestation (i.e. not Claim) on a dead human to form a compound being that isn't at all similar to how the Claimed work mechanically.<br /> The only reason I would recommend Geist 2e is if you want to read up on the difference between ghosts and geister, and want to know more about the Underworld. But if your idigam only snatches ghosts that are just lingering in the living world then there's really no need.<br /> <br /> What you need to create ghosts is the ephemeral entity creation rules that are available in many 2e core books. It's almost identical to that of the spirit creation rules in WtF 2e except that in Werewolf they simply removed the parts that had to do with ghosts.<br /> If you have the CofD core book, Mage 2e core book or Promethean 2e core book, then you already have the rules. If not, you can get them for free in the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">God-Machine Chronicle Rules Update</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T18:48:22-07:00","id":1408622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408468#post1408468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't bother with either version of Geist: The Sin-Eaters. The character creation process is not about regular ghosts. It's about a specific subset of ghosts that have used a very different type of Manifestation (i.e. not Claim) on a dead human to form a compound being that isn't at all similar to how the Claimed work mechanically.<br /> The only reason I would recommend Geist 2e is if you want to read up on the difference between ghosts and geister, and want to know more about the Underworld. But if your idigam only snatches ghosts that are just lingering in the living world then there's really no need.<br /> <br /> What you need to create ghosts is the ephemeral entity creation rules that are available in many 2e core books. It's almost identical to that of the spirit creation rules in WtF 2e except that in Werewolf they simply removed the parts that had to do with ghosts.<br /> If you have the CofD core book, Mage 2e core book or Promethean 2e core book, then you already have the rules. If not, you can get them for free in the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">God-Machine Chronicle Rules Update</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfect! Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:05:35-07:00","id":1408690,"title":"","content":"If you want a different version/type/species of Ghost Claimed, there is one in Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, which is a bit more.. vicious, let put it this way. It is made in 1e rules in mind, however, so some conversion may be required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:15:59-07:00","id":1408828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408690#post1408690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a different version/type/species of Ghost Claimed, there is one in Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, which is a bit more.. vicious, let put it this way. It is made in 1e rules in mind, however, so some conversion may be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo... That sounds interesting. I'll have to take a look at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25368-critcat","name":"CritCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:15:02-07:00","id":1409186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1408468#post1408468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't bother with either version of Geist: The Sin-Eaters. The character creation process is not about regular ghosts. It's about a specific subset of ghosts that have used a very different type of Manifestation (i.e. not Claim) on a dead human to form a compound being that isn't at all similar to how the Claimed work mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor correction on this note: While the big selling point about Geists is their ability to develop and use the Bound Manifestation that constitutes the Bound splat, Geists a) can develop the Claim Manifestation, b) don't always develop the Bound Manifestation, and c) aren't always incentivized to use Bound over Claim.<br /> <br /> Bound is appealing for Geists who want to rise in Rank without risking the Rivers again, feel incentivized to resolve their Remembrance as the way to directly resolve their Burden* or other post-life interests, and are open to having a partner in the process.<br /> <br /> Claim is appealing for Geists who don't want to work around another person while dealing with the flesh, don't consider their Remembrance essential to resolving their post-life concerns, and correspondingly either don't feel the need to rise in Rank or summarily lack the fear of the Rivers as a means to do so.<br /> <br /> I didn't bring it up in LostLight's Ghost Are People Critique thread, but the sort of Bad Geists that thread was asking questions about are more likely to be incentivized by Claim over Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-19-2020, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:54:04-07:00","id":1409195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1409186#post1409186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor correction on this note: While the big selling point about Geists is their ability to develop and use the Bound Manifestation that constitutes the Bound splat, Geists a) can develop the Claim Manifestation, b) don't always develop the Bound Manifestation, and c) aren't always incentivized to use Bound over Claim.<br /> <br /> Bound is appealing for Geists who want to rise in Rank without risking the Rivers again, feel incentivized to resolve their Remembrance as the way to directly resolve their Burden* or other post-life interests, and are open to having a partner in the process.<br /> <br /> Claim is appealing for Geists who don't want to work around another person while dealing with the flesh, don't consider their Remembrance essential to resolving their post-life concerns, and correspondingly either don't feel the need to rise in Rank or summarily lack the fear of the Rivers as a means to do so.<br /> <br /> I didn't bring it up in LostLight's Ghost Are People Critique thread, but the sort of Bad Geists that thread was asking questions about are more likely to be incentivized by Claim over Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said character creation, which is about the Bound and the Geister that have performed the Bargain. I'm well aware that Geister can have other Manifestations, but those rules are also present in many other rulebooks and OP already said they don't have the 2e core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:19:35-07:00","id":1409203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1408363-ghosts-as-duguthim?p=1409195#post1409195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said character creation, which is about the Bound and the Geister that have performed the Bargain. I'm well aware that Geister can have other Manifestations, but those rules are also present in many other rulebooks and OP already said they don't have the 2e core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, missed that. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}